een Hugo and Cleo.\n5. Hugo sits at one end of the row.\n6. Fitz sits somewhere to the left of Esme.\n7. Esme does not sit in seat 3.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id":5,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [HOfcrYMuOUBwo]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Rotate the string left by 11: move its first 11 characters to the end, in the same order.\n2. Shift every letter forward by 17 places in the alphabet, wrapping from z back to a (and Z back to A); keep each letter's case; leave digits unchanged.\n3. Sort the characters in ascending ASCII order (digits before uppercase letters before lowercase letters).\n4. Keep only the characters at odd positions (the 1st, 3rd, 5th, â€¦, counting from 1).\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"order","id":6,"prompt":"Facts:\n\nThe Hazel file was registered on 28 April 1905.\nThe Alder file was registered on 12 April 1950.\nThe Elm file was registered on 10 March 1991.\nThe Juniper file was registered on 19 June 1910.\nThe Ivy file was registered on 9 March 1953.\n\nList the 5 labels from the latest registration to the earliest.\n\nGive the labels only, in the requested order, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id":7,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [7CpL3vo2MIhRlL]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Sort the characters in ascending ASCII order (digits before uppercase letters before lowercase letters).\n2. Swap the case of every letter (lowercase becomes uppercase and uppercase becomes lowercase); leave digits unchanged.\n3. Keep only the characters at odd positions (the 1st, 3rd, 5th, â€¦, counting from 1).\n4. Reverse the string.\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"logic","id":8,"prompt":"4 people (Fitz, Hugo, Cleo, Bram) sit in a row of 4 seats numbered 1 to 4 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. Cleo does not sit at either end of the row.\n2. Cleo does not sit in seat 1.\n3. Hugo and Fitz do not sit next to each other.\n4. Bram sits in seat 2.\n5. Fitz sits immediately to the left of Bram.\n6. Cleo sits in seat 3.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"order","id":9,"prompt":"Facts:\n\nThe Dogwood crate weighs 25,565 kg.\nThe Elm crate weighs 91,811 kg.\nThe Birch crate weighs 5,390 kg.\nThe Ivy crate weighs 71,663 kg.\nThe Alder crate weighs 72,174 kg.\n\nList the 5 labels from the heaviest crate to the lightest.\n\nGive the labels only, in the requested order, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id":10,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [RFiDyxdYjCw7CQ]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Reverse the string.\n2. Rotate the string left by 6: move its first 6 characters to the end, in the same order.\n3. Swap the case of every letter (lowercase becomes uppercase and uppercase becomes lowercase); leave digits unchanged.\n4. Replace every occurrence of the character J with s (case-sensitive).\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANS